  "issue_number": 28,
  "issue_title": "Add issue bot and PR bot for repository governance",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\nAdd lightweight repository automation for issue triage and PR governance.\n\nThis repo is moving toward a competition-style contribution flow, so the first automation priority should be deterministic repository policy checks rather than model-side or infra-heavy workflows.\n\n## Problem\n\nIssue and PR handling is still mostly manual.\n\nThat causes a few recurring problems:\n- inconsistent issue quality\n- missing reproduction details or benchmark scope\n- PRs touching scoring or evaluation paths without early visibility\n- extra maintainer time spent on labeling, routing, and policy checks\n\n## Goal\n\nAdd an issue bot and a PR bot to improve contributor guidance and reduce maintainer overhead.\n\nThe automation should be deterministic and repository-focused.\n\n## Proposed scope\n\n### Issue bot\n- auto-label issues by type and area\n- comment when required details are missing\n- ask for benchmark, affected file/path, repro steps, and expected behavior\n- escalate scoring or protocol-related issues for maintainer review\n\n### PR bot\n- validate PR template completion\n- auto-label PRs by changed paths\n- detect risky changes in scoring, evaluation, benchmark adapters, and frozen configs\n- post a short risk summary comment\n- request maintainer review on sensitive paths\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- no AI review bot\n- no automatic benchmark evaluation\n- no auto-merge\n- no OpenRouter, GPU, or remote-run dependencies\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- issues are auto-labeled and missing-info issues receive a guidance comment\n- PRs are auto-labeled from changed paths\n- PRs touching sensitive files are flagged automatically\n- PR template compliance is checked in automation\n- all bot behavior is deterministic and local to GitHub workflows or scripts\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-10T13:06:54.000Z",
